      "id": "part_03-ch_11",
      "position": 14,
      "kind": "chapter",
      "prefix": "Chapter 11",
      "title": "Pingxi Sky Lanterns: Whispers Rising to the Clouds",
      "summary": "In the misty mountain valley of Taiwan, thousands release glowing paper lanterns inscribed with brush-painted dreams into the nocturnal skies.",
      "content": "![Luminous constellation of thousands of amber lanterns ascending over Taiwanese valleys](https://assets.lingocafe.app/traditions-01/images/pingxi-sky-lanterns-wishes-clouds-hero.webp)\n\nNestled among the rain-soaked gorges of New Taipei City, the village of Pingxi was once an isolated outpost frequented by banditti during the Qing dynasty. To signal that peril had passed and mountain refuges were secure, villagers released primitive hot-air lanterns fabricated from oiled paper and bamboo splints. Over centuries, this pragmatic defensive semaphore evolved into the Pingxi Sky Lantern Festival (*Tianyideng*), an aesthetic communion between earthly aspirations and the celestial void.\n\nConstructing a *tian deng* is an act of communal deliberation. Artisans mount gossamer sheets of mulberry paper onto tensile bamboo frames, forming polygonal domes nearly two meters tall. Visitors dip ink-laden brushes into slate stones to write four-character idioms (*chengyu*), health supplications, and personal vows across the translucent parchment. At the base, a pack of joss paper soaked in flammable tallow is secured with wire.\n\n![Calligrapher painting black ink characters onto delicate rice paper lanterns](https://assets.lingocafe.app/traditions-01/images/pingxi-sky-lanterns-wishes-clouds-detail.webp)\n\nWhen ignited, convective physics transforms the paper envelope into a buoyant vessel of radiant gold. In synchronized releases conducted on the town's school grounds, thousands of lanterns launch simultaneously, ascending through low-hanging mountain mist. The visual effect is mesmerizing: an artificial aurora of amber light drifting upward against emerald peaks, carrying collective human longings into the quiet sanctuary of the cosmos."
